WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.259
When you're at the controls of a giant franchise,
you can't please everybody and this seems

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:07.729
to go double for Star Wars fans.

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:13.389
Disney CEO Bob Iger took a philosophical approach
to fans' dissatisfaction with the sequel trilogy

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:18.260
during a conversation with Variety at the
Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker premiere.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.410
Iger acknowledged that, while the creative
minds behind the series tried to be mindful

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:27.199
of what fans wanted, they were also aware
of the fine line between fan service and simple

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:28.199
pandering.

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:31.820
"We don't overreact to that, we respect fans
of Star Wars, that's really important to us,

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.710
to Lucasfilm, to the franchise.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.510
But we do the best job we possibly can."

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.230
Iger expressed his own satisfaction with the
job that his filmmakers had done on the sequels,

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:46.390
including J.J. Abrams, who as the co-writer
and director of The Rise of Skywalker had

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:52.190
the unenviable task of bringing the nine-film
Skywalker Saga to a close in a way that would

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:57.080
be true to all of the movies that came before,
while still giving fans everything they wanted

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.470
and telling his own unique story.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:04.830
“We've done a really good job of threading
that needle, walking that fine line.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.439
We respect our fans, but we don't overreact
to it either."

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:12.140
Brace yourself for a shock: many fans and
critics disagree.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.560
One of the common complaints about Rise of
Skywalker has concerned its willingness to

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.439
indulge in fan service at the expense of its
story, which can be seen as course-correction

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:25.710
away from the daring narrative choices made
in the series' previous installment, The Last

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:26.710
Jedi.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.700
While that film was one of the best-reviewed
in the entire series, it supremely divided

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:35.999
fans some of whom now feel that Abrams has
swung too far back in the opposite direction.

00:01:35.999 --> 00:01:40.900
Another pervasive gripe: that Rise of Skywalker
was illustrative of the fact that the trilogy

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.729
as a whole lacked a unified vision, which
may be why there has recently been talk of

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:49.469
future Star Wars movies straying away from
the trilogy format.

00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:53.689
Lucasfilm President Kathleen Kennedy suggested
as much during an interview with the Los Angeles

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:56.570
Times the weekend before the release of Episode
IX.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:57.570
She said,

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:02.359
"I think [focusing on single films] gives
us a more open-ended view of storytelling

00:02:02.359 --> 00:02:04.880
and doesn't lock us into this three-act structure.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.660
We're not going to have some finite number
and fit it into a box.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:11.200
We're really going to let the story dictate
that."

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.030
Iger, however, implied that her comments should
be taken with a grain of salt.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.490
"Oh, I don't know about that.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.940
She and I have said, 'Well, maybe trilogies
are too hard, so maybe we'll make one film

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.700
and then a sequel,' but we don't know."

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.700
Of course, it's likely that some observers
will take this as yet further evidence that

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.640
the stewards of Star Wars lack a clear vision
for the property but even the staunchest critics

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:37.640
would have to agree that the House of Mouse
hasn't done everything wrong.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.700
"So, I'm, still in command…?"

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.370
In fact, one thing has gone very, very right
for Disney's Star Wars endeavors of late:

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:50.260
The Mandalorian, the Disney+ series that has
drawn critical raves, helped amass millions

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:55.280
of subscribers for the nascent streaming service,
and launched a bonafide pop culture icon in

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:00.060
"the Child," the adorable character better
known to fans and the world at large as Baby

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.060
Yoda.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.290
Iger admitted that, while he obviously had
high hopes for the series' success, even he

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.800
was blindsided by its rapturous reception.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:13.750
"I think it would be wrong for me to say I
knew exactly how everybody would react because

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.820
it's been huge, but I did have a strong sense
it was a character people were going to love."

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.790
Perhaps The Mandalorian could help provide
some guidance for Disney and Lucasfilm brass

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:28.150
on how to effectively engage fans going forward
that is, beyond "put Baby Yoda in everything,"

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.620
which we honestly wouldn't have much of a
problem with.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.350
Season 2 of the series is currently in production,
and if creator/showrunner Jon Favreau is able

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:39.730
keep fans hooked, Iger and Kennedy would do
well to take a good hard look at how they

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:43.680
could apply some of his Mando magic to future
Star Wars films.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.540
"I gotta get one of those."

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.100
Of course, they've also reached out for a
little help from across the hall; in a development

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.790
which the Star Wars faithful have simply got
to be pumped about, it was announced in September

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.410
that Marvel boss Kevin Feige who has had just
a little bit of success in developing beloved

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:03.910
properties for the big screen to the utter
delight of fans has been tapped to help develop

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.970
a new Star Wars picture.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:05.970
"This will begin to set things right."

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:09.490
While we won't see the fruits of this arrangement
for quite some time, that's okay Iger has

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:13.510
made it clear that Disney won't be rushing
any new Star Wars flicks to market after The

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:18.199
Rise of Skywalker, but will instead place
the property on a 2 or 3 year hiatus while

00:04:18.199 --> 00:04:20.190
the direction of the franchise is worked out.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:21.699
"We'll see about that."

00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:25.730
All of which is to say that while the sequel
trilogy may not have been exactly what everybody

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:29.219
hoped for, the future of Star Wars still looks
reasonably bright.

00:04:29.219 --> 00:04:34.289
Also, it must be said: the Mouse House may
not have fielded a perfect trio of films,

00:04:34.289 --> 00:04:37.360
but hey, they were better than the prequels,
right?

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.740
"I'm not sure I understand."

